Cell["\<\
Uses the points in the first crystal cell to identify the number of sites and \
split each hopping matrix into site-to-site internal blocks.\
\>", "Notes",
 CellID->194499428,ExpressionUUID->"0260eac6-2c8d-514d-9af8-a70a644e001f"],

Cell["\<\
After removing zero matrices, examines only effective displacement keys \
absent from the original nonzero hopping association. It does not search for \
newly enabled bonds within an already present key.\
\>", "Notes",
 CellID->203419619,ExpressionUUID->"7211e349-baab-0e4e-8a25-3f43862267e3"],

Cell["\<\
If no new nonzero key is found, returns originalCutoff. Otherwise returns the \
maximum site-pair distance identified at those new keys.\
\>", "Notes",
 CellID->952734330,ExpressionUUID->"dc30a7cc-0ec3-c749-ab6e-bb56e335f049"],

Cell["\<\
Option \"ZeroThreshold\" defaults to 1.*^-5 and controls the numerical zero \
test. Effective matrices must have the reduced internal dimension appropriate \
to the supplied crystal basis.\
\>", "Notes",
 CellID->1451518341,ExpressionUUID->"62084979-2ff1-414f-80bb-b68c0f2921cc"]
}, Closed]],

